# VelaGuard TTS streaming refactor — code facts

All paths under repo root `/home/hello19y/openvela/contest2026_004_TeamFalcons` (app code `app/velaguard/`). Transport types live outside the contest repo in `/home/hello19y/openvela/packages/ai_agent/`.

## 1. TTS receive path — `app/velaguard/vg_voice_cloud.c`

Whole file is gated `#if defined(CONFIG_VG_VOICE_LOOPBACK) &amp;&amp; defined(CONFIG_EXAMPLES_AI_AGENT_VELA)` (vg_voice_cloud.c:13, ends :1295).

**`struct vc_tts_sink`** — vg_voice_cloud.c:713-734, verbatim:

```c
struct vc_tts_sink
{
  uint8_t *pcm;
  size_t   pcm_len;
  size_t   pcm_cap;
  char  *line;
  size_t line_len;
  size_t line_cap;
  char  *payload;
  size_t pcm_bytes;
  bool   done;
  int    error;
  const agent_llm_timing_t *timing; /* send-done anchor once posting starts */
  uint32_t t0;                      /* fallback anchor: pre-post instant */
  bool   first_line_seen;
  uint32_t first_line_ms;
  bool   first_pcm_seen;
  uint32_t first_pcm_ms;
  uint32_t block_ms[VC_TTS_OBS_MAX];
  uint8_t block_count;
  uint32_t last_block_ms;
};
```

**PCM accumulation buffer**: yes, 512 KB. `#define VC_PCM_MAX_BYTES (512u * 1024u)` at vg_voice_cloud.c:704. It is **heap** (`realloc`), not static: `vc_tts_pcm_reserve` (vg_voice_cloud.c:764-802) grows from 32 768 doubling up to the cap; `need &gt; VC_PCM_MAX_BYTES` logs `"tts: reply over %u bytes"` and returns -1 (776-780). The sink is zeroed and grown once at request start (vg_voice_cloud.c:1072-1077).

**SSE line buffer**: `VC_SSE_LINE_INIT 32768`, `VC_SSE_LINE_MAX 524288` (vg_voice_cloud.c:40-41); `vc_tts_grow` (859-887) doubles `line` and `payload` together; overflow logs `"tts: SSE line over %u bytes"` and sets `error` (1004-1013). Other sizes: `VC_PCM_CHUNK 16384` (:42), `VC_PCM_SAMPLES 15360` (:43, multiple of 3 for the 3:2 resampler).

**Sink callback `vc_tts_write`** (vg_voice_cloud.c:976-1019) — this is the `vela_resp_sink_t.write`. Feeds byte-by-byte; on `'\n'` calls `vc_tts_line`; returns 1 when `done` (verified-complete contract of `vela_resp_sink_t`, agent_http.h:80-88), -1 on error.

**`vc_tts_line`** (vg_voice_cloud.c:889-974):
- Calls `vg_sse_line_data(s-&gt;line, s-&gt;line_len, s-&gt;payload, s-&gt;line_cap)` (:900). That helper (vg_voice_pcm.c:583-624) trims CR/LF, requires prefix `data:` (optional one space), returns **1** = payload, **0** = non-data line, **-1** = `[DONE]` (exact 6-byte match at vg_voice_pcm.c:611-614), **-2** = payload too big for buffer.
- `rc == -1` ([DONE]) → `s-&gt;done = true; return 0` (vg_voice_cloud.c:903-907). `rc == -2` → -1 (error) (:909-911).
- First data line timestamp: `first_line_seen/first_line_ms` (914-919).
- JSON: `choices[0].delta.audio.data` base64 → `vc_tts_emit_pcm` (922-968); `finish_reason == "stop"` also sets `done` (:939-941).
- Block observation (950-964): every audio-bearing line is one "block"; first `VC_TTS_OBS_MAX = 16` (:711) arrival offsets kept in `block_ms[]`, plus `block_count` and `last_block_ms` for the whole reply.

**Base64 decode helper**: `vc_tts_emit_pcm` (vg_voice_cloud.c:804-857) decodes in whole-base64-group steps into a 16 KB stack buffer using `vg_b64_decode` (vg_voice_pcm.c:524-581; returns bytes written or -1). On first non-empty append records `first_pcm_seen/first_pcm_ms` (843-849).

**Anchor math**: `vc_tts_anchor` (vg_voice_cloud.c:741-749) prefers `timing-&gt;send_done_mono` (transport-recorded absolute ms at body-send-done) and falls back to `sink.t0` = pre-post `agent_mono_ms()` (set at :1088). `agent_llm_timing_t` has `int32_t first_data_ms; uint32_t send_done_mono; /* 0=unknown */` (packages/ai_agent/src/infra/agent_timing.h:79-80) and `AGENT_T_NA (-1)` (:50).

**Completion vs truncation classification** — vg_voice_cloud.c:1142-1165:
- transport error or sink error (:1142-1152): `agent_http_cancelled` → `VG_VC_CANCELLED`; `AGENT_HTTP_ERR_TIMEOUT` or deadline expired (`agent_http_stop`) → `VG_VC_TIMEOUT`; `sink.error != 0` → `VG_VC_FORMAT`; else `vc_from_transport` (:65-73: CANCELLED/TIMEOUT, everything else `VG_VC_NET`).
- `status != 200` → `VG_VC_HTTP` (:1154-1158).
- **Truncation check** (:1160-1165): `sink.pcm_bytes == 0 || (pcm_bytes &amp; 1) || sink.line_len != 0 || !sink.done` → `VG_VC_FORMAT`. So a stream that ended without `[DONE]`/`finish_reason:stop` (or with a half-accumulated line, odd byte count, or nothing) is classified `VG_VC_FORMAT`, same code as malformed JSON. There is currently no distinct "truncated" result code.
- Success additionally re-checks the deadline at :1263-1266 (CANCELLED/TIMEOUT even after a full write).

Full `enum vg_vc_result` + names: vg_voice_cloud.h:49-61, names in `vg_vc_result_name` (vg_voice_cloud.c:47-63).

## 2. `vg_voice_cloud_tts` full flow

Signature — vg_voice_cloud.c:1021-1023 (decl vg_voice_cloud.h:93-95):

```c
enum vg_vc_result vg_voice_cloud_tts(const char *text, const char *wav_out,
                                     const vela_req_ctl_t *ctl,
                                     struct vg_vc_info *info);
```

- `wav_out == NULL` → defaults to `VG_VC_TTS_WAV_PATH` (:1030). Request body built at :1065-1070: `{"model":"&lt;CONFIG_VG_VOICE_TTS_MODEL&gt;","messages":[{"role":"assistant","content":"&lt;escaped&gt;"}],"audio":{"format":"pcm16","voice":"&lt;CONFIG_VG_VOICE_TTS_VOICE&gt;"},"stream":true}`; text escaped by `vc_json_escape` (:272-328). Posted via `vc_post(false, ...)` → `agent_http_post_stream_timed` (:440-441), with the fixture detour `agent_http_probe_post_stream` under `CONFIG_VG_VOICE_TEST_FIXTURE` (:423-436).
- **Resample step** (:1167-1257): decoded PCM is 24 kHz mono in `sink.pcm`. Batches of `VC_PCM_SAMPLES` (15 360) are copied out, `vg_pcm_resample_24k_16k(pcm_in, got, pcm_out, VC_PCM_SAMPLES*2)` (decl vg_voice_pcm.h:47-48, impl vg_voice_pcm.c:256-303 — ratio 3:2, linear interpolation, 24 k→16 k). Stereo duplication happens **inside the WAV writer**: `vg_pcm_writer_write` (vg_voice_pcm.c:337-376) writes each mono sample twice (`frames[2*i] = frames[2*i+1] = mono[i]`). Comment at vg_voice_cloud.c:1167-1169: "Convert 24 kHz mono to the 16 kHz stereo the player was verified with."
- **WAV writing**: `vg_pcm_writer_open(&amp;w, out_path, out_total)` (:1196) with `out_total = (samples / 3u) * 2u` (:1176); the writer writes a 44-byte 16 kHz stereo header up front (`wav_header(hdr, 2, 16000, samples*4)`, vg_voice_pcm.c:326) and `vg_pcm_writer_close` fails with -EIO if `written != expected` (vg_voice_pcm.c:397-400) — a short file is an error, not silence. Writer struct `struct vg_pcm_writer { void *f; size_t expected; size_t written; }` (vg_voice_pcm.h:57-62).
- **Cancel during conversion**: loop checks `agent_http_stop(ctl, now_ms)` each batch (:1204-1213) and breaks with `VG_VC_CANCELLED`/`VG_VC_TIMEOUT`.
- **Cleanup** (`out:` label :1268-1285): `unlink(VG_VC_TTS_PCM_PATH)` always (:1274 — file is vestigial; nothing writes it in this version), `unlink(out_path)` when `rc != VG_VC_OK` (:1276-1279), then frees `sink.line`, `sink.payload`, `sink.pcm`, `body`. `vg_voice_cloud_cleanup` (:1288-1293) unlinks `VG_VC_CLIP_PATH`, `VG_VC_CLIP_MONO_PATH`, `VG_VC_TTS_PCM_PATH`.
- **`struct vg_vc_info`** — vg_voice_cloud.h:63-70:

```c
struct vg_vc_info
{
  int      status;       /* HTTP status, 0 when no reply */
  uint32_t req_bytes;
  uint32_t resp_bytes;
  uint32_t audio_bytes;  /* TTS: PCM before resampling */
  uint32_t elapsed_ms;
};
```

## 3. Playback path — `vr_stage_tts` in `app/velaguard/vg_voice_round.c`

Function spans vg_voice_round.c:801-904. Flow:

1. `ctl.deadline_ms = g_vr.s.deadline_ms; ctl.cancel = &amp;g_vr.cancel` (:807-808). Then a `vg_agent_round_voice_reserve()` wait loop (20 ms poll) :811-817.
2. `rc = vg_voice_cloud_tts(g_vr.s.answer, VG_VC_TTS_WAV_PATH, &amp;ctl, &amp;info)` (:824). Log line `[vgvoice] tts rc=... status=... pcm=... resp=... ms=...` (:826-828), `vr_log_stage("tts_end")` (:829).
3. Cancel checks unlink the WAV and return 0 (:831-835, :844-848). `rc != OK` → `vg_vs_tts_result(..., false, ...)` → state RESULT with `speech_failed=true` (:837-842; vg_voice_session.c:330-357).
4. **Post playback**: `vg_voice_play_file(VG_VC_TTS_WAV_PATH)` (:851) — just posts `REQ_PLAY` onto the audio worker's request ring (vg_voice.c:976-992); returns 0 when queued, non-blocking. On failure → unlink + tts_result(false) (:850-855).
5. `first_playable` marker: syslog `[vgvoice] first_playable gen=%u elapsed_ms=%u` (elapsed from `g_vr.s.submit_ms`) at :857-858, then `vr_log_stage("play_posted")` at :859 — this is the "first audio handed to the player" point, not first audible sample.
6. **Completion wait** (:863-903) — this is the block to be replaced by consumed-byte counting:

```c
uint32_t limit = 60000;
struct stat st;
if (stat(VG_VC_TTS_WAV_PATH, &amp;st) == 0 &amp;&amp; st.st_size &gt; 44)
  {
    /* 16 kHz stereo 16-bit: 64000 bytes per second. */
    limit = (uint32_t)((st.st_size - 44) / 64) + VR_PLAY_EXTRA_MS;
  }
bool idle = false;
uint32_t started = vr_now_ms();
while (!g_vr.cancel &amp;&amp; vr_now_ms() - started &lt; limit)
  {
    if ((idle = vr_wait_voice_idle(100))) break;
  }
bool completed = idle;
if (!idle)
  {
    vg_voice_cancel();
    idle = vr_wait_voice_idle(2000);
  }
if (idle) unlink(VG_VC_TTS_WAV_PATH);
```

   Upper bound = WAV data bytes / 64 (B/s) + `VR_PLAY_EXTRA_MS 5000u` (defined :61); default 60 s when stat fails. Poll: `vr_wait_voice_idle` (:221-224) is `vg_voice_wait_idle` (vg_voice.c:1016-1028) — polls every 10 ms (`usleep(10000)`) for `state == VG_VOICE_IDLE &amp;&amp; !voice_pending()`, false on FAULT.
7. On completion: `vr_log_stage("play_done")` (:899) + `vg_vs_play_done(&amp;g_vr.s, gen, now)` (:900; vg_voice_session.c:359-375 → state RESULT, `VG_VS_ACT_SHOW_RESULT`). Incomplete/`last_result != VG_VOICE_OK` → `vg_vs_tts_result(..., false, ...)` (:892-893).

**Player instance**: one global in the audio worker — `static struct nxplayer_s *g_player;` (vg_voice.c:117), created lazily in `voice_play_path` (vg_voice.c:523-532) with `nxplayer_create()`, `nxplayer_setdevice(g_player, "/dev/audio/pcm0p")`, `nxplayer_setvolume(g_player, VOICE_PLAY_VOLUME /* 900 */)`, then `nxplayer_playfile(g_player, path, AUDIO_FMT_UNDEF, AUDIO_FMT_UNDEF)` (vg_voice.c:541). `voice_play_path` also probes the WAV and rejects duration &gt; 60 000 ms with -EFBIG (vg_voice.c:534-539). Stop path: `voice_stop_playback` (vg_voice.c:446-466) sends `AUDIO_MSG_STOP` via `mq_timedsend` with 1 s deadline and waits bounded `VOICE_STOP_MS 3000u` (:40) for `voice_player_done()` (427-444: player state IDLE, `dev_fd &lt; 0`, thread joined).

**WAV path and deletion**: `VG_VC_TTS_WAV_PATH` = `VG_VOICE_DIR "/tts-16k.wav"` (vg_voice_pref.h:38), `VG_VOICE_DIR` default `"/data/velaguard/voice"` (vg_voice_pref.h:25-27, overridable for host tests). Deleted: on cancel in `vr_stage_tts` (:833, :847, :853), after successful wait (:887), and by `VG_VS_ACT_RELEASE_AUDIO` (`vg_voice_round.c:1058-1064`, issued by `vg_vs_end`, vg_voice_session.c:511-514).

## 4. Session / thread model

**Two threads**:

- **Voice round worker (pthread)**: `vr_thread` (vg_voice_round.c:1074-1167), created in `vg_voice_round_start` (:1196-1203) with `pthread_attr_setstacksize(&amp;attr, VR_STACK_SIZE)`; `#define VR_STACK_SIZE 49152` (:57, comment :54-56 explains 48 KB covers mbedTLS handshake + ASR body builder ~10 KB frames). **`VR_PRIORITY 118` (:58) is defined but never applied** — only stacksize is set, so the pthread inherits the creator's priority. Tick: `sem_timedwait` with `VR_TICK_MS 50` timeout (:59, :1080-1092). Runs everything: record start/stop requests, ASR (including the RAM clip handoff), agent round wait, the cloud TTS call, and the playback wait loop. Wake sources: button callback `vr_button` (:198-214, only posts flags + `sem_post`), overlay commands (`end_pending` :1116-1121, `retry_pending` :1123-1129), hold/mute (:1134-1146), and `vg_vs_tick` (:1156-1157).
- **Audio worker (task)**: `task_create("vgvoice", CONFIG_VG_VOICE_PRIORITY, CONFIG_VG_VOICE_STACKSIZE, voice_task, NULL)` (vg_voice.c:835-836). Kconfig defaults: `VG_VOICE_PRIORITY` = 110 (Kconfig:232-240), `VG_VOICE_STACKSIZE` = 4096 (Kconfig:242-246); neither overridden in `scripts/configs/velaguard-lvgl.defconfig` (no such lines). Runs PDM decimation (`voice_drain`, vg_voice.c:253-289), WAV writes (`voice_write_wav`, :375-420), NxPlayer playback and its completion detection (`voice_player_done` polled in the task loop :769-783), plus the `REQ_TAKE_PCM` RAM handoff (:688-705).

**Round lifecycle / submit anchor**: `vg_vs_release` (vg_voice_session.c:162-193) sets `s-&gt;submit_ms = now_ms; deadline_ms = now_ms + VG_VS_BUDGET_MS` (30 000, vg_voice_session.h:33; retry budget 15 000, :34) and returns `STOP_RECORD | START_ASR`. `vr_elapsed_ms` (vg_voice_round.c:113-123) is `now - g_vr.s.submit_ms`; `vr_log_stage` (:125-129) prints `[vgvoice] stage=%s t=%u`. Stage names seen: `asr_begin` (:247), `asr_end` (:298), `asr_wait_recorder` (:1002), `agent_begin` (:621), `tool_direct` (:641), `agent_queued` (:695), `agent_reply` (:727), `facts_end` (:572/:770), `tts_begin` (:821), `tts_end` (:829), `play_posted` (:859), `play_done` (:899). Settle markers: `round_settled` (:504-509), `cancel_settled` (:511-521).

**`vg_agent_round_voice_reserve`**: declared vg_agent_round.h:88-93 ("ASR 开始前暂停后台并保留请求，失败或取消也必须 release"); defined vg_agent_round.c:228-250 — suspends a running background `ADVICE`/`DAILY` round (copies request aside, `velaclaw_client_abandon(g_client)`, bumps `g_request_serial`), sets `g_voice_foreground = true`, returns 0; returns `-EBUSY` if the outstanding round is owned by VOICE or is not suspendable. While `g_voice_foreground`, other owners are refused in `round_queue` (vg_agent_round.c:161-163). Used at: `vr_stage_asr` (vg_voice_round.c:237-243) and `vr_stage_tts` (:811-817) — both poll it every 20 ms until 0; released in `vr_show_result` (:525), `vr_show_error` (:538), and `VG_VS_ACT_HIDE_OVERLAY` (:1048). Purpose per comment vg_agent_round.c:227: keep ASR upload from competing with the background model on the network.

**Recording start/stop**: start = `vg_voice_record_begin_owned(&amp;gen)` (vg_voice.c:936-950, posts `REQ_BEGIN` without `archive_wav` → RAM-only, no WAV file) → `voice_start` (vg_voice.c:477-512): `stm32_pdm_capture_start(VG_VOICE_RATE_HZ, g_ring, sizeof(g_ring), voice_capture_cb, NULL)` (:501-502), ISR callback `voice_capture_cb` (:210-251) copies DMA halves into an 8-slot block queue. Stop = `voice_finish` (vg_voice.c:566-663): first line is

```c
int ret = stm32_pdm_capture_stop(50);   /* vg_voice.c:569 */
```

That **50 is a bounded timeout in ms, not a fixed sleep**: `stm32_pdm_capture_stop(unsigned int wait_ms)` (nuttx/boards/arm/stm32h7/stm32h750b-dk/src/stm32_bringup.c:569-577) → `stm32_sai_capture_stop(g_pdm_i2s, wait_ms)` (nuttx/arch/arm/src/stm32h7/stm32_sai.c:2445). The SAI driver stops the DMA, then spins on 1 µs polls up to `wait_ms*1000` µs for the DMA+SAI-enable handshake, returning `-ETIMEDOUT` if it doesn't clear (stm32_sai.c:2492-2508); `wait_ms == 0` would use the driver default `SAI_CAPTURE_STOP_WAIT_MS 50` (stm32_sai.c:2290, 2483-2486). So the "suspected ~50 ms budget" is an upper bound on the hardware disable handshake + tail-half handover, typically faster. After it: `voice_drain` (:578), stats, and either WAV write (local path) or publish IDLE (cloud path, :661-662).

**`CONFIG_VG_VOICE_LOOPBACK`** (Kconfig:209-228) gates far more than loopback: the entire audio worker `vg_voice.c` (include guard vg_voice.c:9), the NSH tool `vgvoice.c` (:19), and — together with `CONFIG_EXAMPLES_AI_AGENT_VELA` — `vg_voice_cloud.c` (:13) and `vg_voice_round.c` (:19). It depends on `VG_BRINGUP_TOOLS &amp;&amp; VG_PTT &amp;&amp; AUDIO &amp;&amp; I2S &amp;&amp; STM32H7_SAI_CAPTURE &amp;&amp; STM32H7_SAI1_A &amp;&amp; STM32H7_SAI_PDM_MODE &amp;&amp; SYSTEM_NXPLAYER` (Kconfig:212-214). `vgvoice.c` additionally guards its cloud commands with `CONFIG_EXAMPLES_AI_AGENT_VELA` (vgvoice.c:33, :201).

## 5. `VG_VOICE_TLS_CACHE`

- **Kconfig**: app/velaguard/Kconfig:248-254 — `bool "Experimental TLS session cache for voice"`, `default n`, `depends on EXAMPLES_AI_AGENT_VELA`. Help (translated): "Diagnostic session-resumption cache. Disabled by default after a full-handshake signature-verification failure occurred; to be re-enabled after independent validation of its long-term lifecycle."
- **Gated code**: `/home/hello19y/openvela/packages/ai_agent/src/infra/vela_tls.c`, all sites `#if defined(CONFIG_VG_HMI) &amp;&amp; defined(CONFIG_VG_VOICE_TLS_CACHE) &amp;&amp; defined(MBEDTLS_SSL_CLI_C)` — lines 488, 1250, 1325, 1346, 1353.
- **What it caches**: an mbedTLS **TLS 1.2 session for resumption**, in RAM only, for exactly one target — `host == "token-plan-cn.xiaomimimo.com" &amp;&amp; port == "443"` (`tls_voice_session_target`, vela_tls.c:499-503). State (vela_tls.c:490-496): `static mbedtls_ssl_session voice_session; static pthread_mutex_t voice_session_lock; static pthread_once_t voice_session_once; static bool voice_session_valid; static uint32_t voice_session_saved;`
- **Lifecycle**: `tls_voice_session_offer` (vela_tls.c:515-533) calls `mbedtls_ssl_set_session` before handshake, expiring the entry after 60 000 ms; `tls_voice_session_save` (535-549) stores the session only when the negotiated version is exactly `"TLSv1.2"`; an offered session that then fails handshake is cleared (`if (session_offered) tls_voice_session_clear();` at ~1325); success logs `[..] voice session offered=%u handshake_ms=%u` (~1346-1350). Design comment at :487: "仅对 HMI 已知服务的受控连接缓存 TLS 1.2 会话，恢复资格一分钟后失效。不保存到文件，不缓存 HTTP 凭据；服务端可拒绝恢复并执行完整握手。"
- **Why default-off**: the Kconfig help — when resumption was offered, the server path produced full-handshake signature-verification failures; re-enable is pending separate validation. Also note the surrounding DNS-count reset hard-codes the same host at vela_tls.c:479-485.
- Host test compiled **with** it enabled: `test_tls_voice_session` uses `-DCONFIG_VG_HMI -DCONFIG_VG_VOICE_TLS_CACHE` (host_tests/Makefile:256-257).

